    {# ===== featured — Jacobin, told as their story ===== #}
    <section class="py-[60px] border-t border-ink/[0.07]">
    <div class="max-w-[1180px] mx-auto px-7">
      <p class="{{ eyebrow }} text-flame">The full story</p>

      <article class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-ink/15 bg-night-2 mt-[26px]">
        <div class="{{ phin }} aspect-[16/10] min-h-[320px] border-b border-ink/15">
          <img class="w-full h-full object-cover object-center" src="/img/jacobin/jacobin-social.png" alt="Jacobin Social, a federated comment section for the German edition of Jacobin magazine" />
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 min-[901px]:grid-cols-[1.4fr_.6fr]">
          <div class="px-[30px] py-8">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 flex-wrap mb-3">
              <span class="font-smono text-[.66rem] tracking-[.12em] uppercase text-flame">A magazine · Independent media</span>
              <span class="{{ origin }}">◼ Co-designed with us</span>
            </div>
            <h2 class="font-disp font-[560] text-[clamp(1.5rem,2.8vw,2.1rem)] leading-[1.06] mb-4">Jacobin: From audience to community</h2>

            <div class="{{ goal }} mb-[18px]">
              <div class="{{ goallab }}">What they were after</div>
              <p class="m-0 font-disp font-medium text-[1.18rem] leading-[1.3]">Readers who debate, organise and build solidarity together — not an audience that reacts to articles and leaves.</p>
            </div>

            <p class="text-ink-2 text-base m-0">A comment section was never going to do that, and neither was sending readers to a platform someone else owns. So they kept publishing on Ghost and gave the <b class="text-ink font-semibold">conversation a home they control</b> — federated, in their own brand, with the groups and boundaries their community actually needed. Six months later, 3,000+ readers have a space that answers to them.</p>

            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-6">
              <a class="{{ btnfire }}" href="/case-studies/jacobin/">Read the full story</a>
              <a class="{{ btnline }}" href="https://jacobin.social" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit jacobin.social ↗</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <aside class="px-7 py-8 bg-night-3 border-t border-ink/15 min-[901px]:border-t-0 min-[901px]:border-l">
            <div class="grid gap-[13px]">
              <div class="border-b border-ink/[0.07] pb-[11px]"><div class="{{ goallab }} mb-0">Community</div><div class="text-[.96rem] mt-1"><b class="font-disp font-semibold">Jacobin</b> — German edition</div></div>
              <div class="border-b border-ink/[0.07] pb-[11px]"><div class="{{ goallab }} mb-0">People</div><div class="text-[.96rem] mt-1"><b class="font-disp font-semibold">3,000+</b> readers</div></div>
              <div class="border-b border-ink/[0.07] pb-[11px]"><div class="{{ goallab }} mb-0">Live since</div><div class="text-[.96rem] mt-1">July 2026</div></div>
